			<div class="content" id="post-content-3864266">
									

<p>I really liked this one right up until the ending.<br />
I was with you all the way but the last bit after the population percentage logs felt flat and kind of out of place for me.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;contains&nbsp;spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>In the last part SCP-4000-1A says basically the exact same thing shes already said once before, only for some unexplained this time it convinces Dr Hardcastle to follow her which I thought was very out of character considering her speech about not believing in anything.</p>
<p>It's a no vote from me but I would have upvoted if it ended after the O5 council were converted, for me that would have felt more like a more realistic punchy ending.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Also I'd suggest removing <strong>Addendum 3&#160;23/01/28</strong>, it doesn't add anything in terms of world building or plot, even after finding out the true functionality of SCP-4000 this part just seems like additional unnecessary information on random D-class just for the sake of padding.</p>

							</div>

								
